From 8c342b16d4ce118cdbffde98dbc542d8f08bc9d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:48:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show how to skip the gym's and the battle's tallies
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

While the stats a training session or a battle gave count up, and then the battle's bits, a row at the bottom of the box
that counts says "Press × to skip" (patch 0333, the owner's proposal E): the gym's stats box (TRN and TRN2) grows by a
row under a divider like the battle box's; in battle the bits box grows by a row under the end text's panel, or under
the bits row where there is no end text, so the text is never moved or covered. The row shows from the moment the boxes
open, when the skip is already taken, until nothing counts or a skip was asked; the box keeps its size after. The
button is the one that confirms: × in blue, and with JAPANESE CONTROLS the font draws it as ○ (modButtonGlyph), in the
red of the PlayStation's ○ (FONT_CLUT 3), per glyph through drawFittedRow. The line is drawn once into the evolution
hint's row of the text area when the box opens (main.QOL_STR_SKIP_COUNT, in all eight languages). Nothing counts: the
boxes are as before. The count itself is unchanged.
